            "paragraph": "CMIP5 vs. CMIP6: The transition from CMIP5 to CMIP6 models has improved the simulation of regional climate extremes, particularly in South Asia and other drought-prone areas. Indices that incorporate temperature and evapotranspiration (e.g., SPEI, MSDI) demonstrate greater sensitivity and reliability under high-emission scenarios (SSP5-8.5), where temperature-driven droughts are projected to increase in both frequency and severity.",
